rsx draw engine: WPOS counts pixels on an antialiased target held at its sample grid.

The engine keeps a DIAGONAL_CENTERED_2 / SQUARE_*_4 colour target at its sample resolution and maps the viewport over
it, so the pixel program runs once per sample and SV_POSITION counts samples; the RSX runs it once per pixel and WPOS is
the pixel's window position. A program that addresses a screen-sized texture by WPOS then reads it at twice the
position. Resistance 3's scene buffer is a 960x640 2x1 target and its material pass fetches the light and SSAO buffers
by WPOS: the left half of the frame was lit from the wrong place (doubled, translucent-looking figures, wrong
shadows) and the right half clamped to the buffers' edge column (full-width horizontal streaks).

rsx_fp_apply_wpos_grid (beside rsx_fp_apply_unnorm_scale) rewrites a program that reads WPOS so every sample gets the
centre of its pixel, floor(pos / grid) + 0.5; programs without WPOS and 1x1 targets stay byte-identical. The engine
applies it for a non-1x1 grid, which also joins the pipeline key.

test_fp_decompiler: the rewrite on single and MRT entry points, no-ops (1x1, no WPOS), short buffer, applied twice.
test_rsx_draw_engine: a WPOS program on CENTER_1 / DIAGONAL_CENTERED_2 / SQUARE_CENTERED_4 / SQUARE_ROTATED_4 targets.
Scripted run: Home level, turn to the near rock wall: bands gone (band score 12 -> 2.7), ghosts gone.

Upstream: PR #446 (rsx_live_draw and the Vulkan backend render AA targets the same way and could apply the same
helper).

